OL,3,GNEWSAVictorian railway station left    
OL,4,Auntouched for 70 years goes on sale    
OL,5,Awith suitcase still inside             
OL,7,FA Victorian-era railway station is up  
OL,8,Ffor sale at #135,000 after being left  
OL,9,Fempty for more than 70 years.          
OL,11,FHolland Arms station in Pentre Berw was
OL,12,Fthe second stop on the defunct Anglesey
OL,13,FCentral Railway line that ran from the 
OL,14,Fvillage of Gaerwen to the port town of 
OL,15,FAmlwch.                                
OL,17,FOpened to the public on 12 March 1865, 
OL,18,Fthe station has been disused for       
OL,19,Fdecades after closing in 1952 and bears
OL,20,Frelics of its past, including rusted   
OL,21,Fsignal lamps and a cobweb-covered      
OL,22,Fsuitcase.                              
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
